cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "HydroTuring: a conservation-law benchmark for AI hydrologic models"
message: "If you use HydroTuring, please cite it and record the suite version. Scores are only comparable within a suite version."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Zhi
    family-names: Li
    affiliation: University of Colorado Boulder
    email: chrimerss@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/chrimerss/HydroTuring"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  HydroTuring tests whether an AI-based hydrologic model conserves mass,
  energy and momentum, rather than whether it fits a hydrograph. Forcing is
  generated at run time from a recorded seed, so there is nothing to
  memorise. Every probe must demonstrably separate a physically exact
  reference model from models that close the budget by construction, that
  hide a silent sink, or that reach closure through a degenerate partition.
keywords:
  - hydrology
  - benchmark
  - machine learning
  - conservation laws
  - water balance
  - physics-informed
